---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

/**
 * This section is the one place the full technical range is stated. Keep the
 * hero and section leads free of capability lists so nothing repeats.
 *
 * Photo is picked up automatically. Drop a file at `src/assets/profile.jpg`
 * (.jpeg, .png and .webp also work) and it appears; with no file present the
 * text runs full width.
 */
const matches = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
  '../assets/profile.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp}',
  { eager: true }
);
const photo = Object.values(matches)[0]?.default;
---

<div class:list={['about', photo && 'about--with-photo']}>
  {
    photo && (
      <div class="about__photo">
        <Image
          src={photo}
          alt={SITE.name}
          widths={[240, 480]}
          sizes="(min-width: 46rem) 208px, 160px"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    )
  }

  <div class="about__text">
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Theodor, a Unity developer and architect based in Romania, with 14 years building
      games across PC, mobile, TVs and VR.
    </p>

    <p>
      Much of my focus sits with the underlying systems: real-time and turn-based multiplayer,
      network communication and optimisation, and
      server-authoritative designs that keep the server the source of truth so clients cannot
      influence outcomes. Alongside that, system design grounded in established patterns and coding
      principles, and the implementation, extension and adaptation of the plugins and frameworks a
      team depends on.
    </p>

    <p>
      An equal share of my experience is operational: feature flagging, phased rollouts, A/B
      testing, content updates and tuning, all of which continue well beyond release. I care as much
      about the codebase as the people building it, and whether leading a team or working as an
      embedded contributor, I bring the same focus on solid architecture, clear communication and
      genuine ownership of what ships.
    </p>

    <p>
      AI tools like Claude Code have become a core part of how I work, helping me plan better, catch
      issues earlier, and think problems through before writing a line of code.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside of work, games remain a long-standing personal interest and a large part of why the
      industry still holds my attention. I'm always happy to discuss game architecture, multiplayer
      systems, or where AI-assisted development is heading.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about--with-photo {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 13rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .about__photo :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .about__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .about--with-photo {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .about__photo {
      max-width: 10rem;
    }
  }
</style>
